      "result": "Revision 3 is written, but it has not been run \u2014 I had no execution tool, so all checks are marked NOT RUN by author in `interface_report.md`. Nothing is committed, and no change was written outside the allowed candidate files.\n\n**Fixes against review_02**\n1. **Water connection is now mandatory.** `propose_withdrawal` refuses unless the session has both an explicit `DayBinding` and an initial resource cursor. You supply them in `start(..., day_binding=, initial_resource=)`, or later through the new `stage_connect_water`. A session without them is transport-only. `read_availability` also refuses states without a completed daily lineage, so legacy or no-daily states no longer pass just because they are interevent. A read with no run/ordinal or a pending storm is refused by the session, as before.\n2. **Extra physical T debits are refused.** Every later read and every checkpoint pairing must carry the same `request_sequence` and `n_requests` as LEAF has consumed. Hydrology, close and storm states with the same T counts are still accepted. A pending-after-debit save now checks that plan, proposal and accepted identity/before/after are consistent with the consumed history, and that `external == after`.\n3. **Operator association is checked.** `resource_identity` requires a genuine `LifecycleOperator`, SYRUP's own minted-state check, and `parent.lop_sha256 == lop.sha256`. It records the parent's hash rather than the passed one.\n4. **Memory preflight.** `start` and restore now check a metadata-only lower bound before any status mask or copy. It counts every plant as live and adds root resource scratch. I also added a public `PlantSession.memory_ledger()` so Codex can compare the structural estimates against measured peaks.\n5. **Tests.**\n   - Stale-flush now uses an independent branch.\n   - The tight-cap test calls the real `start` entry point with `tracemalloc` instead of mocking call order.\n   - Reproduction tests use a one-patch fixture and keep `max_new_plants=5`; a separate test covers the capacity refusal.\n   - Regressions added for binding, extra-T, wrong operator, pending-save mismatches, and CPU/numba/CUDA checkpoint, rollback and parity.\n   - The 12 real-native tests are kept, with the explicit initial resource added.\n\n**Divergence from C1.** I extended `rebuild_geometry` in `leaf/biocalendar.py`, so it is no longer byte-identical to C1. The canopy builder now gets `min(canopy cap, global max_bytes)`, with live caller reserve, candidate state, root map and area counted as its reserve. This changes memory accounting only; no scientific kernel was touched, and `growth.py` and `plant_pet.py` remain byte-identical. It needs your requalification.\n\n**Remaining limits**\n- Everything is unexecuted, so syntax or API-shape errors are possible. Inferred pieces include `uptake.estimate_map_bytes`, the `RootMap` and `PlantState._arrays` usage, the Phase 2/3 evaluator return keys and the shipped Phase 2/3 fixture catalogs.\n- I read the headers and docs of `demography.py` and `recruitment.py`, but not the bodies of `decide`, `evaluate_event` or `evaluate`. The Phase 2/3 delegation still rests on the call patterns I read in `IntereventSession`.\n- Memory figures are conservative structural estimates, not measurements.\n- LEAF cannot independently verify that MASY supplied the right `DayBinding` origin and initial resource.\n\nT off with growth on stays refused.",
